# Slice 420, step 1 (LMX_semantics.en.md:614: the root declarations of the data provide the inputs, the code's root
# declarations the remaining locals; :208, `int: x` with no value only checks its contract and writes nothing): a root
# place of the code that its data declares holds the data's value from the entry, in both executors; the write into the
# data is explicit (`data\x`).  Over a named Structure and over a formal (split_formal_data).  Entry 7; 81.. name the
# failing check.
D:
    int: x 1
S:
    int: x
    data\x := x + 1
fn: over_formal (@: d D) int
    call(d S)
    return: 0
fn: over_named () int
    call(D S)
    return: D\x
int: code 7
if: over_named() != 2
    code := 81
int: dropped over_formal(D)
if: code = 7 && D\x != 3
    code := 82
send: exit(exit_code: code; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
